<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leo von Klenze</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1784–1864</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo von Klenze was a German neoclassical architect and court architect of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-i-of-bavaria">Ludwig I of Bavaria</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> he built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glyptothek">Glyptothek</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alte-pinakothek">Alte Pinakothek</a>, the Ruhmeshalle and much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwigstrasse">Ludwigstrasse</a>, and near Regensburg the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walhalla">Walhalla</a>, a Greek-style temple of German worthies. He also designed the New Hermitage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg">Saint Petersburg</a> and advised on the planning of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leo-von-klenze.jpg" alt="Leo von Klenze" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Hanfstaengl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leo_von_Klenze_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
